    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>
      The <code style="font-size: .8em; background: none; border: 0; padding: 0">quorum</code> crate
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The decision core of the shrinking quorum. Each tick it decides what the system may deliver, given what three
      replicas returned.
    </p>
    <div class="row" style="gap: 8px; margin: 8px 0 24px">
      <span class="pill">no_std</span>
      <span class="pill">no allocation</span>
      <span class="pill">no dependencies</span>
      <span class="pill sig">
        <span class="dot"></span>9 Kani proofs
      </span>
      <span class="pill">v0.3.1</span>
    </div>

    <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
    <p>The crate is not on crates.io yet. Depend on the repository at a tag:</p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0"><span class="c"># Cargo.toml</span>
[dependencies]
quorum = {'{'} git = <span class="s">"https://github.com/mruspace/flight"</span>, tag = <span class="s">"v0.3.1"</span> {'}'}</pre>

    <h2 id="example">Example</h2>
    <pre
      class="pre"
      tabindex="0"
    ><span class="k">use</span> quorum::{'{'}decide, Health, Outcome, Policy, Reply, REPLICAS{'}'};

<span class="c">// read_replicas, send and run_known_answer_test are your code.</span>
<span class="k">let mut</span> health = Health::new();
<span class="k">for</span> tick <span class="k">in</span> 0u64.. {'{'}
    <span class="k">let</span> replies: [Reply; REPLICAS] = read_replicas(tick);
    <span class="k">let</span> v = decide(Policy::Shrink, &amp;replies);

    <span class="k">if let</span> <span class="s">Outcome::Deliver</span>(x) = v.outcome {'{'} send(x); {'}'}
    <span class="k">for</span> (i, outvoted) <span class="k">in</span> v.dissent.iter().enumerate() {'{'}
        <span class="k">if</span> *outvoted &amp;&amp; health.strike(i, tick) {'{'} run_known_answer_test(i); {'}'}
    {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>

    <h2 id="gate">Gate commands on the mode</h2>
    <p>
      On one replica, self-check can deliver a few wrong results before the periodic known-answer test catches a stuck
      fault. Use that mode for data products, not spacecraft commands, unless the mission adds its own command safety
      layer. This example issues a command only when the mode is <code>Vote</code> or <code>Compare</code> and the
      outcome is <code>Deliver</code>. See <a href="/concepts/shrinking-quorum/#command-path">Command path</a>.
    </p>
    <pre
      class="pre"
      tabindex="0"
    ><span class="c">//! Gate commands on the mode. Only a result that two or more replicas agree</span>
<span class="c">//! on (vote or compare) may command the spacecraft. A result from the last</span>
<span class="c">//! replica&#39;s self-check goes out as a data product only.</span>
<span class="k">use</span> quorum::{'{'}decide, Mode, Outcome, Policy, Reply, REPLICAS{'}'};

<span class="c">/// What to do with one tick&#39;s result.</span>
<span class="k">enum</span> Action {'{'}
    <span class="c">/// Agreed by two or more replicas: may be used as a command.</span>
    Command(u64),
    <span class="c">/// Self-check on the last replica: data product only.</span>
    Data(u64),
    <span class="c">/// Nothing to send this tick.</span>
    Hold,
{'}'}

<span class="k">fn</span> gate(replies: &amp;[Reply; REPLICAS]) -&gt; Action {'{'}
    <span class="k">let</span> verdict = decide(Policy::Shrink, replies);
    <span class="k">match</span> (verdict.mode, verdict.outcome) {'{'}
        (Mode::Vote | Mode::Compare, Outcome::Deliver(x)) =&gt; Action::Command(x),
        (Mode::SelfCheck, Outcome::Deliver(x)) =&gt; Action::Data(x),
        _ =&gt; Action::Hold,
    {'}'}
{'}'}

<span class="k">fn</span> main() {'{'}
    <span class="k">use</span> Reply::{'{'}Absent, Pair, Single{'}'};
    <span class="k">let</span> ticks = [
        [Single(7), Single(7), Single(9)], <span class="c">// vote: two agree on 7</span>
        [Absent, Single(7), Single(7)],    <span class="c">// compare: both say 7</span>
        [Absent, Single(7), Single(9)],    <span class="c">// compare: mismatch</span>
        [Absent, Absent, Pair(7, 7)],      <span class="c">// self-check on the last replica</span>
        [Absent, Absent, Absent],          <span class="c">// nothing left</span>
    ];
    <span class="k">for</span> replies <span class="k">in</span> &amp;ticks {'{'}
        <span class="k">match</span> gate(replies) {'{'}
            Action::Command(x) =&gt; println!("{'{'}replies:?{'}'}: command {'{'}x{'}'}"),
            Action::Data(x) =&gt; println!("{'{'}replies:?{'}'}: data product {'{'}x{'}'}"),
            Action::Hold =&gt; println!("{'{'}replies:?{'}'}: hold"),
        {'}'}
    {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      Its output, from <code>cargo run</code> against v0.3.1:
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">[Single(7), Single(7), Single(9)]: command 7
[Absent, Single(7), Single(7)]: command 7
[Absent, Single(7), Single(9)]: hold
[Absent, Absent, Pair(7, 7)]: data product 7
[Absent, Absent, Absent]: hold</pre>

    <h2 id="api">API</h2>
    <h3>const REPLICAS: usize = 3</h3>
    <p>Number of replicas.</p>
    <h3>const STRIKES: usize = 3</h3>
    <p>
      Strikes within <code>STRIKE_WINDOW</code> ticks that trigger a diagnosis.
    </p>
    <h3>const STRIKE_WINDOW: u64 = 200</h3>
    <p>Length of the strike window, in ticks.</p>

    <h3>enum Policy</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Shrink</td>
            <td>Vote on three, compare on two, self-check on one.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Tmr</td>
            <td>Vote on three, compare on two, stop on one (classic fixed TMR).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>enum Mode</h3>
    <p>
      <code>Vote</code>, <code>Compare</code>, <code>SelfCheck</code> (one replica computes everything twice and
      compares with itself), <code>Halted</code>.
    </p>

    <h3>enum Reply</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Absent</td>
            <td>The replica is dead or did not answer.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Single(u64)</td>
            <td>One result.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Pair(u64, u64)</td>
            <td>Two results of the same computation (self-check).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>enum Outcome</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr class="hl">
            <td class="m">Deliver(u64)</td>
            <td>Deliver this result.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Detected</td>
            <td>A disagreement was caught; deliver nothing this tick.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Halted</td>
            <td>The policy cannot continue with the replicas left.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>struct Verdict</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">mode</td>
            <td class="m">Mode</td>
            <td>The mode used this tick.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">outcome</td>
            <td class="m">Outcome</td>
            <td>What to do with this tick.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">dissent</td>
            <td class="m">[bool; 3]</td>
            <td>Replicas that were outvoted (vote mode only).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">diagnose</td>
            <td class="m">bool</td>
            <td>
              Two replicas disagree and nothing tells which is wrong: run a known-answer test on both (shrinking quorum
              only).
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>fn mode(policy, alive) -&gt; Mode</h3>
    <p>
      The mode a policy runs in with <code>alive</code> live replicas.
    </p>
    <h3>fn decide(policy, &amp;[Reply; 3]) -&gt; Verdict</h3>
    <p>Decide what to deliver from the replicas&#39; replies.</p>
    <h3>struct Health</h3>
    <p>
      Strike record per replica. <code>Health::new()</code> is <code>const</code>. <code>strike(i, tick)</code> returns{' '}
      <code>true</code> when replica <code>i</code> has three strikes inside the window and must be diagnosed.{' '}
      <code>clear(i)</code> forgets its strikes after it passes. <code>to_raw()</code> and{' '}
      <code>Health::from_raw(strikes, count)</code> turn the record into plain arrays and back, to save it across a
      reset or hand it to C.
    </p>
    <p>
      From C or C++, use the <a href="/core/fprime/#c">C interface</a>, <code>quorum.h</code>. Kani proves that{' '}
      <code>quorum_mode</code>, <code>quorum_decide</code>, <code>quorum_health_strike</code> and{' '}
      <code>quorum_health_clear</code> give this crate&#39;s answer.
    </p>

    <h2 id="proofs">Kani proofs</h2>
    <p>
      Nine proofs: four on the core in <code>quorum</code>, five on the C interface in <code>quorum-ffi</code>. CI runs
      <code>cargo kani -p quorum -p quorum-ffi</code> on every change. In the core proofs, each reply is any of
      <code>Absent</code>, <code>Single</code> or <code>Pair</code>, with any <code>u64</code> values.
    </p>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Proof</th>
            <th>Property</th>
            <th>Scope</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum/src/lib.rs#L331">
                identical_while_tmr_can_run
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>With two or more replies present, both policies give the same outcome.</td>
            <td>
              Every set of three replies with two or more present. Outcome only, not mode or <code>diagnose</code>.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum/src/lib.rs#L343">tmr_stops_below_two</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              With fewer than two replies present, fixed TMR&#39;s outcome is <code>Halted</code>.
            </td>
            <td>Every set of three replies with fewer than two present.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum/src/lib.rs#L352">
                shrink_halts_only_with_nothing_left
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              The shrinking quorum&#39;s outcome is <code>Halted</code> if and only if no reply is present.
            </td>
            <td>Every set of three replies.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum/src/lib.rs#L362">
                delivers_only_agreed_values
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              A delivered value has two agreeing replies, or exactly one replica alive that returned{' '}
              <code>Pair(v, v)</code>.
            </td>
            <td>Every set of three replies, under both policies.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum-ffi/src/lib.rs#L314">decide_is_the_core</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>quorum_decide</code> gives the core&#39;s verdict. An unknown reply kind counts as absent.
            </td>
            <td>C interface: policy 0 or 1, any reply kind and values.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum-ffi/src/lib.rs#L330">bad_policy_halts</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              Any other policy code halts <code>quorum_decide</code> and <code>quorum_mode</code>.
            </td>
            <td>C interface: any policy code above 1.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum-ffi/src/lib.rs#L340">mode_is_the_core</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>quorum_mode</code> gives the core&#39;s mode.
            </td>
            <td>
              C interface: policy 0 or 1, any <code>u32</code> count.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum-ffi/src/lib.rs#L359">strike_is_the_core</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>quorum_health_strike</code> gives the core&#39;s answer and record. A replica above 2 changes
              nothing.
            </td>
            <td>
              C interface: any record with counts in the <code>u32</code> range, any replica and cycle.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.3.1/quorum-ffi/src/lib.rs#L384">clear_is_the_core</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>quorum_health_clear</code> gives the core&#39;s record. A replica above 2 changes nothing.
            </td>
            <td>
              C interface: any record with counts in the <code>u32</code> range, any replica.
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="tiny">Each proof name links to its source at v0.3.1.</p>
    <h3 id="not-covered">Not covered</h3>
    <ul class="sig-list">
      <li>
        <strong>
          <code>Health</code> in the core.
        </strong>{' '}
        Unit tests only.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Diagnosis and the known-answer test.</strong> They run in the demo and in F&#180;, not in the core.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Timing.</strong> The proofs say what <code>decide()</code> returns, not how long it takes. The
        <a href="/core/bench/#core">bench</a> measures that.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The system over a run.</strong> Never less than fixed TMR over a whole run is tested, not proved. See
        <a href="/concepts/shrinking-quorum/#tested">Tested (per run)</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="targets">Targets and builds</h2>
    <p>CI builds and tests on every change:</p>
    <ul class="sig-list">
      <li>Linux ARM64, Linux x86_64 and macOS (Apple silicon)</li>
      <li>
        Bare-metal ARM Cortex-M, <code>thumbv7em-none-eabihf</code>, as <code>no_std</code> (build only)
      </li>
      <li>Static ARM Linux binaries of the demo, 64-bit and 32-bit (hard and soft float), tested under emulation</li>
    </ul>
    <DocsEnd />
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
